  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21526498",
      "title": "Handling Error Responses",
      "lectureOrder": 164,
      "videoOrder": 142,
      "sourceHash": "ae1627845c10b9e9c8429e89383c011e4e7f171c9a797abb782073d121b3c517",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 3.09,
          "en": "Now, there's one more thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.09,
          "end": 5.63,
          "en": "you gotta know related to that though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.63,
          "end": 9.38,
          "en": "The fetch method works such that technically, errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.38,
          "end": 13.06,
          "en": "like the one I generated with the invalid URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.06,
          "end": 17.513,
          "en": "are in the end handled with this catch method like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.88,
          "end": 21.84,
          "en": "You also could be errors that are stemming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.84,
          "end": 26.84,
          "en": "from the server site, so that are stemming from Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.14,
          "end": 29.17,
          "en": "which are not technically errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.17,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "So where you do get a regular response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 36.5,
          "en": "but the response simply tells you that something went wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.5,
          "end": 39.34,
          "en": "And that would by default not be handled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.34,
          "end": 40.593,
          "en": "with this catch block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.49,
          "end": 43.99,
          "en": "And I can show this to you as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.99,
          "end": 46.29,
          "en": "Let me show you a server site error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.29,
          "end": 47.42,
          "en": "And that's something I can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.42,
          "end": 49.92,
          "en": "in the LearningSurvey.vue file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.92,
          "end": 52.25,
          "en": "Here, we're sending the data and there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.25,
          "end": 55.48,
          "en": "we are actually not using then or a catch at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.48,
          "end": 57.7,
          "en": "I'm not using then because I don't care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.7,
          "end": 61.02,
          "en": "about the response here, but I actually should care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.02,
          "end": 63.293,
          "en": "about whether everything worked or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.43,
          "end": 67.37,
          "en": "So I also wanna show the user an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.37,
          "end": 69.143,
          "en": "if sending the data failed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.47,
          "end": 74.44,
          "en": "For that, of course, we can add an error property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.44,
          "end": 77.05,
          "en": "to data here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.05,
          "end": 80.67,
          "en": "And then simply add a catch method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.67,
          "end": 83.163,
          "en": "to wait for a potential error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.13,
          "end": 86.08,
          "en": "And if we do get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.08,
          "end": 90.35,
          "en": "we can set this.error equal to something went wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.35,
          "end": 93.13300000000001,
          "en": "Try again later or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.66,
          "end": 97.55,
          "en": "And I wanna reset it right before we start fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.55,
          "end": 99.663,
          "en": "Here, I'll set error to null again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.71000000000001,
          "end": 106.663,
          "en": "So now we also handle errors here in the send data case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.63,
          "end": 110.22,
          "en": "and we can use the error property now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.22,
          "end": 114.02000000000001,
          "en": "for example, here to show an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.02000000000001,
          "end": 116.27000000000001,
          "en": "Of course, you could also instead show an alert,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.27000000000001,
          "end": 118.47999999999999,
          "en": "whatever you wanna do, but here I'll check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.47999999999999,
          "end": 123.48,
          "en": "if error is truthy, if it is an error string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.53,
          "end": 125.663,
          "en": "and in that case, I output the error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.04,
          "end": 131.743,
          "en": "And now, of course, I can generate the same error as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.94,
          "end": 135.06,
          "en": "if I remove the .json here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.06,
          "end": 137.423,
          "en": "Now in the case for sending data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.63,
          "end": 143.17000000000002,
          "en": "If I do that and I try to send data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.17000000000002,
          "end": 145.593,
          "en": "I eventually get this error output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.46,
          "end": 149.253,
          "en": "But that's just technically error I was talking about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.47,
          "end": 155.14,
          "en": "But now let me show you another kind of error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.14,
          "end": 157.81,
          "en": "an error which will not be a technical error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.81,
          "end": 160.04,
          "en": "thrown by the browser but instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.04,
          "end": 162.29,
          "en": "an error generated by the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.29,
          "end": 165.09,
          "en": "which is then still resulting in a regular response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.09,
          "end": 168.65,
          "en": "being sent back, but a response which is not okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.65,
          "end": 170.84,
          "en": "but which instead has a status code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.84,
          "end": 173.84300000000002,
          "en": "that indicates that something went wrong on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.77,
          "end": 177.2,
          "en": "And we can force Firebase to do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.2,
          "end": 180.65,
          "en": "by removing .json stringify.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.65,
          "end": 182.84,
          "en": "With that, we're telling Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.84,
          "end": 184.39,
          "en": "that we're sending .json data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.39,
          "end": 188.07,
          "en": "and that is what we should send and what Firebase expects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.07,
          "end": 191.73,
          "en": "But then we're actually sending a JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.73,
          "end": 193.663,
          "en": "which is not .json data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.81,
          "end": 199.81,
          "en": "If we do that, reload and try to submit a new rating,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.8,
          "end": 203.56,
          "en": "we'll see nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.56,
          "end": 205.47,
          "en": "Here, we see no error message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.47,
          "end": 207.69,
          "en": "but if I load my submitted experiences,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 207.69,
          "end": 211.52,
          "en": "the new rating, which I just submitted is not there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.52,
          "end": 213.37,
          "en": "I can do this as often as I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.37,
          "end": 214.35,
          "en": "It's not there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 214.35,
          "end": 216.65,
          "en": "And it's all done out here in Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.65,
          "end": 219.2,
          "en": "The error, we just have the old rating from before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.04,
          "end": 223.92000000000002,
          "en": "We can see the problem if I open the developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 223.92000000000002,
          "end": 226.91,
          "en": "we got an error here, failed to load request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.91,
          "end": 230.62,
          "en": "The server responded with a status of 400.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.62,
          "end": 232.07,
          "en": "And that's the important part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 232.07,
          "end": 235.28,
          "en": "Now it's not a technically error thrown by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.28,
          "end": 238.41,
          "en": "which we had before, but it's a regular response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 238.41,
          "end": 241.86,
          "en": "which just has a status code of 400.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.86,
          "end": 246.373,
          "en": "Success responses always have status codes of 200 or 201.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.53,
          "end": 252.32,
          "en": "If you have 400-ish or a 500-ish responses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.32,
          "end": 254.313,
          "en": "that means something went wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.51,
          "end": 258.47,
          "en": "And that can happen but the problem is catch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.47,
          "end": 260.6,
          "en": "is not picking it up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.6,
          "end": 263.26,
          "en": "Well, that's just how this fetch methods works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 263.26,
          "end": 267.673,
          "en": "We need to add then and have a look at our response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.75,
          "end": 272.36,
          "en": "This then function here will always be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 272.36,
          "end": 274.44,
          "en": "if we have a regular response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.44,
          "end": 276.623,
          "en": "so if we don't have a technical error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.62,
          "end": 280.45,
          "en": "And here we can check if the response is okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 280.45,
          "end": 284.32,
          "en": "and then do something, but if it's not okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 284.32,
          "end": 288.92,
          "en": "which it will not be if we have a 400 or 500 status code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 288.92,
          "end": 292.15999999999997,
          "en": "then I wanna also set my error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.15999999999997,
          "end": 295.02,
          "en": "We could this by setting this.error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.02,
          "end": 297.46,
          "en": "but we could also do this by throwing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.46,
          "end": 299.683,
          "en": "a new error object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.56,
          "end": 304.02,
          "en": "Could not save data, could be the message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.02,
          "end": 305.233,
          "en": "which I pass to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 306.16,
          "end": 308.76,
          "en": "The argument you pass to the error constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 308.76,
          "end": 311.223,
          "en": "is the message that will be set for the error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.72,
          "end": 317.04,
          "en": "And this error constructor here is built into JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 317.04,
          "end": 319.16,
          "en": "This throws a new error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 319.16,
          "end": 322.573,
          "en": "and this will then automatically reach this catch block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 323.86,
          "end": 327.06,
          "en": "And here I can then actually set this.error equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 327.06,
          "end": 330.883,
          "en": "to error.message to use my message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 332.64,
          "end": 336.61,
          "en": "The message property will be present on this error object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 336.61,
          "end": 340.3,
          "en": "because this error constructor creates such an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 340.3,
          "end": 342.90999999999997,
          "en": "where what you pass here will be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 342.90999999999997,
          "end": 344.323,
          "en": "on a message property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 346.09000000000003,
          "end": 348.89,
          "en": "And if we do that and save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 348.89,
          "end": 352.17,
          "en": "if I now reload and try doing this again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 352.17,
          "end": 354.6,
          "en": "now we see Could not save data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 354.6,
          "end": 357.68,
          "en": "And now we're showing the users some message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 357.68,
          "end": 360.25,
          "en": "that allows the user to, well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 360.25,
          "end": 363.073,
          "en": "at least try again later or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 364.62,
          "end": 367.13,
          "en": "Now here, of course, the problem is a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 367.13,
          "end": 369.07,
          "en": "we, as a developer, should avoid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 369.07,
          "end": 372.23,
          "en": "I should stringify this but in reality,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 372.23,
          "end": 376.17,
          "en": "you could have circumstances where the server generates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 376.17,
          "end": 380.91,
          "en": "such an error response without you, as developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 380.91,
          "end": 384.76,
          "en": "the front end, the Vue developer being responsible for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 384.76,
          "end": 386.98,
          "en": "That's why this still was a great example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 386.98,
          "end": 389.94,
          "en": "even though that, of course, in reality would not occur,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 389.94,
          "end": 392.12,
          "en": "but it shows you how you can handle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 392.12,
          "end": 394.703,
          "en": "such service site error responses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 395.71,
          "end": 398.76,
          "en": "And with that, we really handle everything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 398.76,
          "end": 400.87,
          "en": "We handle success cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 400.87,
          "end": 402.39,
          "en": "We can load data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 402.39,
          "end": 404.96,
          "en": "We can show messages if we have no data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 404.96,
          "end": 407.343,
          "en": "and we can also handle errors.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
